    "level": "moderate",
    "original_problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{(3x+5)^{2}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | ${(3x+5)}^{3}$ |",
    "original_worked_solution": "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)={x}^{3}$ and the denominator $v(x)=(3x+5)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{'}(x)=3{x}^{2},\\,{v}^{'}(x)=6(3x+5).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3{x}^{2}){(3x+5)}^{2}-({x}^{3})(6(3x+5))}{{({(3x+5)}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}{(3x+5)}^{2}-6{x}^{3}(3x+5)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}(3x+5)((3x+5)-2x)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}(x+5)}{{(3x+5)}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
